nvalid data. Additionally, the financial analysis methods should validate the data before performing calculations to prevent errors due to unexpected data formats or missing columns.\n\n### Suggestions on Revision\n1. **Error Handling in `load_csv`:**\n   - Wrap the `pd.read_csv` call in a try-except block to handle `FileNotFoundError` and `pd.errors.EmptyDataError`.\n   - Return an empty DataFrame or raise a custom exception with a descriptive message.\n\n2. **Data Validation in Financial Analysis Methods:**\n   - Before performing calculations in methods like `calculate_moving_average`, `calculate_rsi`, and `calculate_macd`, check if the `self.data` DataFrame contains the required columns (e.g., 'Close').\n   - If the required data is missing, raise a custom exception or return None with a warning message.\n\nImplementing these suggestions will improve the robustness and user experience of the application by preventing unexpected crashes and providing informative error messages.\n\n### Instructions to Fix\n- Update the `load_csv` method in `data_loader.py` to include error handling.\n- Modify the financial analysis methods in `financial_analyzer.py` to check for the presence of necessary data before performing calculations.\n\nLet me know if you need assistance with the implementation or further code reviews.", 'input_size': 8872, 'output_size': 1614, 'has_tool_calls': False, 'stage': 'after'} 
