.\\n\\n   ```bash\\n   python main.py\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Import Financial Data**: Use the import function to load your financial data. Supported formats include CSV, Excel, and more. \\n   - Navigate to the data import section in the UI.\\n   - Select the file and upload it.\\n\\n3. **Select Indicators**: Choose the financial indicators you want to analyze from the available options.\\n   - Check the boxes for indicators like Moving Averages, RSI, MACD, etc.\\n\\n4. **Generate Visualizations**: Once the data is imported and indicators selected, you can generate visualizations.\\n   - Click on the \\"Generate Charts\\" button.\\n   - Review the visual outputs to analyze trends.\\n\\n5. **Review Reports**: After analysis, you can generate reports summarizing your findings.\\n   - Navigate to the reporting section and click on \\"Generate Report\\".\\n\\n6. **Exit the Application**: Once you are done analyzing, exit the application by clicking on the exit button or closing the window.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\nThis software provides a comprehensive solution for financial data analysis. By following this manual, you should be able to set up the environment and utilize the main features effectively. For further assistance, refer to the documentation or contact support.\\n","encoding":"utf-8","mode":"overwrite"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'content': '{\n  "path": "manual/manual.md",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\stocktrends_20260531161347\\\\code_workspace\\\\manual\\\\manual.md",\n  "size": 2701\n}', 'tool_call_id': 'call_v7VfDlTklePKYKkWMmpj6D8m', 'metadata': {'tool_name': 'save_file', 'source': 'Chief Product Officer'}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'The user manual has been successfully created and saved in the `manual` directory. You can find it at the following path:\n\n**manual/manual.md**\n\nThis manual includes an introduction to the software, installation instructions for environmen